\v 9 \w For|strong="H4616"\w* \w there|strong="H3068"\w* \w is|strong="H3068"\w* no faithfulness \w in|strong="H3068"\w* \w their|strong="H3068"\w* \w mouth|strong="H6440"\w*. \w Their|strong="H3068"\w* heart \w is|strong="H3068"\w* destruction. \w Their|strong="H3068"\w* throat \w is|strong="H3068"\w* \w an|strong="H6440"\w* \w open|strong="H6440"\w* tomb. \w They|strong="H3068"\w* flatter \w with|strong="H3068"\w* \w their|strong="H3068"\w* tongue.\
\v 10 Hold \w them|strong="H3588"\w* guilty, \w God|strong="H0369"\w*. Let \w them|strong="H3588"\w* fall \w by|strong="H3559"\w* \w their|strong="H3588"\w* own counsels. Thrust \w them|strong="H3588"\w* \w out|strong="H3559"\w* \w in|strong="H7130"\w* \w the|strong="H3588"\w* multitude \w of|strong="H6310"\w* \w their|strong="H3588"\w* transgressions, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w they|strong="H3588"\w* \w have|strong="H0369"\w* rebelled against \w you|strong="H3588"\w*.\
\v 11 \w But|strong="H3588"\w* let \w all|strong="H7230"\w* \w those|strong="H3588"\w* \w who|strong="H0430"\w* take refuge \w in|strong="H0430"\w* \w you|strong="H3588"\w* rejoice. Let \w them|strong="H5307"\w* always shout \w for|strong="H3588"\w* joy, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w you|strong="H3588"\w* defend \w them|strong="H5307"\w*. Let \w them|strong="H5307"\w* \w also|strong="H0430"\w* \w who|strong="H0430"\w* love \w your|strong="H3588"\w* name \w be|strong="H0430"\w* joyful \w in|strong="H0430"\w* \w you|strong="H3588"\w*.\
\v 12 \w For|strong="H5921"\w* \w you|strong="H3605"\w* \w will|strong="H8034"\w* bless \w the|strong="H3605"\w* righteous. Yahweh, \w you|strong="H3605"\w* \w will|strong="H8034"\w* surround \w him|strong="H5921"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w favor|strong="H0157"\w* \w as|strong="H8055"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w a|strong="H5921"\w* shield. 
\c 6
\p \s1 Ask for help to someone seriously ill in body and soul (First Penitential Psalm)
\p## Ask for help to someone seriously ill in body and soul (First Penitential Psalm)
For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments, upon the eight-stringed lyre. A Psalm by David. 
\v 1 Yahweh, don’t rebuke \w me|strong="H5921"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w your|strong="H5921"\w* anger, neither discipline \w me|strong="H5921"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w your|strong="H5921"\w* wrath.\
\v 2 \w Have|strong="H3068"\w* \w mercy|strong="H3068"\w* \w on|strong="H3068"\w* \w me|strong="H3256"\w*, \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w*, \w for|strong="H3068"\w* \w I|strong="H3068"\w* \w am|strong="H3068"\w* faint. \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w*, heal \w me|strong="H3256"\w*, \w for|strong="H3068"\w* \w my|strong="H3068"\w* bones \w are|strong="H3068"\w* troubled.\
\v 3 \w My|strong="H3068"\w* soul \w is|strong="H3068"\w* \w also|strong="H3068"\w* \w in|strong="H3068"\w* great anguish. \w But|strong="H3588"\w* \w you|strong="H3588"\w*, \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w*—\w how|strong="H3588"\w* long?\
\v 4 Return, \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w*. Deliver \w my|strong="H3068"\w* \w soul|strong="H5315"\w*, \w and|strong="H3068"\w* \w save|strong="H5315"\w* \w me|strong="H5315"\w* \w for|strong="H3068"\w* \w your|strong="H3068"\w* loving kindness’ sake.\
\v 5 \w For|strong="H4616"\w* \w in|strong="H3068"\w* \w death|strong="H5315"\w* \w there|strong="H7725"\w* \w is|strong="H3068"\w* no memory \w of|strong="H3068"\w* \w you|strong="H7725"\w*. \w In|strong="H3068"\w* Sheol,\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Sheol is the place of the dead. \f* \w who|strong="H3068"\w* \w shall|strong="H3068"\w* \w give|strong="H7725"\w* \w you|strong="H7725"\w* thanks?\
\v 6 \w I|strong="H3588"\w* am weary \w with|strong="H3588"\w* \w my|strong="H3588"\w* groaning. Every night \w I|strong="H3588"\w* flood \w my|strong="H3588"\w* bed. \w I|strong="H3588"\w* drench \w my|strong="H3588"\w* couch \w with|strong="H3588"\w* \w my|strong="H3588"\w* tears.\
