A meditation by David, which he sang to Yahweh, concerning the words of Cush, the Benjamite. 
\v 1 \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w*, \w my|strong="H3068"\w* \w God|strong="H3068"\w*, \w I|strong="H0834"\w* take refuge \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w you|strong="H0834"\w*. Save \w me|strong="H5921"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w all|strong="H1697"\w* \w those|strong="H0834"\w* \w who|strong="H0834"\w* pursue \w me|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and|strong="H3068"\w* deliver \w me|strong="H5921"\w*,\
