\p \s1 Complain about a violent enemy and rejoice in divine help
\p## Complain about a violent enemy and rejoice in divine help
For the Chief Musician. A contemplation by David, when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, “David has come to Ahimelech’s house.” 
\v 1 Why do you boast \w of|strong="H1732"\w* mischief, mighty man? God’s loving kindness endures continually.\
\v 2 \w Your|strong="H0935"\w* tongue plots destruction, \w like|strong="H1004"\w* \w a|strong="H0935"\w* sharp razor, working deceitfully.\
\v 3 \w You|strong="H3605"\w* \w love|strong="H2617"\w* \w evil|strong="H7451"\w* more \w than|strong="H3605"\w* good, lying rather \w than|strong="H3605"\w* speaking \w the|strong="H3605"\w* truth. Selah.\
\v 4 \w You|strong="H6213"\w* love all devouring words, \w you|strong="H6213"\w* \w deceitful|strong="H7423"\w* \w tongue|strong="H3956"\w*.\
\v 5 God \w will|strong="H6664"\w* likewise destroy \w you|strong="H1696"\w* forever. \w He|strong="H1696"\w* \w will|strong="H6664"\w* take \w you|strong="H1696"\w* up, \w and|strong="H1696"\w* pluck \w you|strong="H1696"\w* \w out|strong="H7451"\w* \w of|strong="H1696"\w* \w your|strong="H0157"\w* tent, \w and|strong="H1696"\w* root \w you|strong="H1696"\w* \w out|strong="H7451"\w* \w of|strong="H1696"\w* \w the|strong="H0157"\w* land \w of|strong="H1696"\w* \w the|strong="H0157"\w* living. Selah.\
\v 6 \w The|strong="H3605"\w* righteous also \w will|strong="H1697"\w* see \w it|strong="H0157"\w*, \w and|strong="H1697"\w* fear, \w and|strong="H1697"\w* laugh \w at|strong="H0157"\w* \w him|strong="H3605"\w*, \w saying|strong="H1697"\w*,\
\v 7 “Behold, this \w is|strong="H0776"\w* \w the|strong="H1571"\w* man \w who|strong="H0410"\w* didn’t make \w God|strong="H0410"\w* \w his|strong="H1571"\w* \w strength|strong="H5331"\w*, \w but|strong="H1571"\w* trusted \w in|strong="H0776"\w* \w the|strong="H1571"\w* abundance \w of|strong="H0776"\w* \w his|strong="H1571"\w* riches, \w and|strong="H0776"\w* strengthened himself \w in|strong="H0776"\w* \w his|strong="H1571"\w* wickedness.”\
