\p \s1 Desperate complaint of a seriously ill person
\p## Desperate complaint of a seriously ill person
A Song. A Psalm by the sons of Korah. For the Chief Musician. To the tune of “The Suffering of Affliction.” A contemplation by Heman, the Ezrahite. 
\v 1 Yahweh, \w the|strong="H5921"\w* God \w of|strong="H1121"\w* \w my|strong="H5921"\w* salvation, \w I|strong="H5921"\w* \w have|strong="H1121"\w* cried day \w and|strong="H1121"\w* night \w before|strong="H5921"\w* \w you|strong="H5921"\w*.\
\v 2 Let \w my|strong="H3068"\w* prayer enter \w into|strong="H3915"\w* \w your|strong="H3068"\w* \w presence|strong="H5048"\w*. Turn \w your|strong="H3068"\w* ear \w to|strong="H3068"\w* \w my|strong="H3068"\w* \w cry|strong="H6817"\w*.\
\v 3 \w For|strong="H8605"\w* \w my|strong="H0935"\w* soul \w is|strong="H6440"\w* full \w of|strong="H6440"\w* troubles. \w My|strong="H0935"\w* life draws \w near|strong="H6440"\w* \w to|strong="H0935"\w* Sheol.\f + \fr 88:3 \ft Sheol is the place of the dead. \f*\
